# The Windows FASM cross-check binary. CITY.COM (assembled in DOS) is the real
# one and is tracked; CITYW.COM is written by MAKEWIN CHECK only to be compared
# against it.
GAMES/WIRECITY/CITYW.COM
TOOLS/MENU/MENUW.COM
TOOLS/LISTING/LISTINGW.EXE
# the episode script's reconstruction - written by the director's check,
# assembled by TOOLS/MENU/RECON.BAT, compared and thrown away
TOOLS/MENU/RECON.ASM
TOOLS/MENU/RECON.COM

# TASM / TLINK build artifacts
*.OBJ
*.obj
EXAMPLES/*.EXE
*.MAP
*.map
*.LST
*.lst
*.bak

# The workshop's own notebooks: NEXT.md (the cold-start brief) and the
# *TASK.md planning files live in Skill/ and stay OFF the public repo -
# they are session notes between the maintainer and the AI, not
# documentation. The public story lives in README.md and docs/.
Skill/

# ...and the AI harness config for the same reason: skills, launch
# entries and machine-local paths are workshop tooling, not the
# project. (launch.json and the fasm-migration skill leaked into two
# 2026-08 commits before this rule existed - untracked since.)
.claude/

# editor / OS noise
*~
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store

# js-dos bundle staging (the final docs/city.jsdos IS committed for Pages)
docs/.bundle/
docs/city.zip
/.vs

# never let secrets reach the public repo (safety net for git add -A)
.env
.env.*
*.key
*.pem
*.pfx
*.p12
*secret*
*token*
*password*
credentials*

# generated at build time inside SRC (the INSTALL copies ARE committed:
# they are the playable release)
SRC/CITY.DAT
BUILD.LOG
stdout.txt
stderr.txt
GAMES/OWLFLY/res/panel1.psd
LOCAL.BAT

# Wavefront MODELS are sources, not TLINK artifacts - un-ignore them
# (the global *.obj above catches TASM output; res/ holds Blender exports)
!GAMES/*/res/*.obj
!TOOLS/TRAINER.OBJ

# Debug harness: keep the folders, drop the noise (shots, flight logs,
# the compiled exe); sources and scenarios stay tracked
Debug/shots/*
!Debug/shots/.gitkeep
Debug/log/*
!Debug/log/.gitkeep
Debug/FlyDbg.exe

# .NET build output, ANYWHERE. The C# tools (TOOLS\Obj2Inc, TOOLS\Panel2Inc)
# and the relay all leave bin\ and obj\ trees behind, and sixty files of
# MSBuild droppings were riding in the repo until 2026-08-03. Nothing needs
# them: MAKE.BAT runs "dotnet run --project", which builds from source.
# NB this is the DIRECTORY obj\, not the *.obj rule above - that one is for
# TASM output and has its own un-ignores for the Wavefront models.
**/bin/
**/obj/

# WireCityChat: local API key and runtime artifacts stay out of the repo
relay/WireCityChat/settings.local.json
relay/WireCityChat/logs/

# LESSONS\L02 build output. These three are the LESSON'S POINT: the reader
# types MAKE and produces them, and step three deliberately PATCHES
# HELLO.COM in place so it prints WORLD while the source still says HELLO.
# A tracked copy is therefore a copy that changes every time anyone works
# through the lesson - and one of them spent a while saying WORLD.
LESSONS/L02/HELLO.COM
LESSONS/L02/HELLO2.EXE
LESSONS/L02/HEX.COM
# LESSONS\L03 build output, for the same reason as L02's: the reader types
# MAKE and produces it. The lesson's whole shape is that you build it.
LESSONS/L03/PIXEL.COM
# LESSONS\L05 - the table generator's build output. MKSIN.C is the source and
# SINT.INC is tracked because the assembly includes it and the browser bundle
# cannot build it (Open Watcom is not in the repository), but the executable
# and the object file are made on the spot.
LESSONS/L05/MKSIN.EXE
LESSONS/L05/MKSIN.OBJ
# ...and the assembled lessons themselves, for the same reason as L02 and L03:
# the lesson's whole shape is that the reader types MAKE and watches it happen.
LESSONS/L05/TURN.COM
LESSONS/L05/PIVOT.COM
# RECON.ASM is the lecture script replayed into a file by the reconstruction
# check (LESSON.md section 3) and RECON.COM is what the assembler makes of
# it. Both are scratch: written, assembled, compared and thrown away.
LESSONS/L05/RECON.ASM
LESSONS/L05/RECON.COM
LESSONS/L06/PIVOT.COM
LESSONS/L06/CLOCK.COM
LESSONS/L06/CLOCKW.COM
# lesson 6 script reconstruction - written by the check, compared, thrown away
LESSONS/L06/RECON.ASM
LESSONS/L06/RECON.COM
LESSONS/L06/CIRCLE.COM
LESSONS/L04/MATH.COM
# The staged workbench disk - generated by TOOLS/packwb.ps1 from the .INF
# manifests, boot-tested by TOOLS/RUNWB.BAT, packed into docs/workbench_v*.jsdos.
# Always derived, never edited in place.
DISK/
LESSONS/L07/LINE.COM
LESSONS/L07/LINEW.COM
LESSONS/L07/RECON.ASM
LESSONS/L07/RECON.COM

# OWL FLY 4 video. THIS RULE IS TEMPORARY - it expires when the codec is
# frozen, and then the packed .OWV files become ordinary tracked assets.
#
# The reason is churn, not size. Git stores differences, which is why this
# repository's whole history of assembly costs so little. Video has no
# differences to store: change one dithering threshold, repack, and every
# byte is new, so git keeps another whole copy beside the old one, forever,
# in every clone. Developing a codec means twenty of those, and history is
# rewritten rather than deleted - which is not something to do to a public,
# forked repository. The .PNG and .WAV assets already tracked here are binary
# too and cost nothing, because nothing rewrites them; that is exactly what
# the video becomes once the format stops moving.
#
# Until then this holds the recipe - the per-scene manifest, the ffmpeg
# invocation and the C# converter - and SAMPLE.OWV, un-ignored at the end as
# the one short clip that lets the player be tested with no footage at all.
#
# VIDEO/src/ is the source footage, kept beside the work that uses it and
# ignored whole. Where it will eventually be published is still open; until
# that is decided it exists on the maintainer's machine only, so it is NOT
# backed up by being here - see the folder's README.
LAB/OWLFLY4/VIDEO/*.OWV
LAB/OWLFLY4/VIDEO/*.owv
LAB/OWLFLY4/VIDEO/frames/
LAB/OWLFLY4/VIDEO/src/*
GAMES/OWLFLY4/res/video/*.OWV
GAMES/OWLFLY4/res/video/*.owv
GAMES/OWLFLY4/res/video/frames/
!LAB/OWLFLY4/VIDEO/SAMPLE.OWV
!LAB/OWLFLY4/VIDEO/src/.gitkeep

# VESATEST writes its transcript here when run with /A - a diagnostic
# result, not a source file.
LAB/OWLFLY4/VIDEO/VESATEST.LOG
LAB/OWLFLY4/VIDEO/PLAYER.LOG
